[12.711121, "o", "\u001b[2m  \"\"\"Get the raw orders from the sales system.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Two sources:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  - a CSV export (the default), one order per line;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  - the sales API, which answers ``GET /orders`` with a JSON list of the orders\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    placed since the fetch before (it keeps the cursor; an order is handed over\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    once, except that the last ones before a fetch may come again).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  There is no real sales API in this repository. ``local_api`` starts a small\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.711167, "o", "\u001b[2m  stand-in on 127.0.0.1 that serves the orders in the CSV file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \"\"\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ... 381 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
